     1	function futures = predictAgentFutures(track, pYield, valid, opts)
     2	%PREDICTAGENTFUTURES  One track in, two futures out: it yields, or it asserts.
     3	%
     4	%   Task D6, piece 1 of 5. Branch/contingency MPC models exactly two modes, and
     5	%   that is precisely what Stream C's predictor outputs, so there is no third
     6	%   future here and there must not be one.
     7	%
     8	%   WHY TWO AND ONLY TWO
     9	%   A yield future and an assert future bracket the behaviour. Anything the other
    10	%   road user actually does lies between them, so a plan safe under both is safe
    11	%   in fact. Adding a "maybe" future would add cost without adding coverage.
    12	%
    13	%   WHY THE PROBABILITY IS NaN WHEN THE PREDICTION IS INVALID
